        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0618" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/230</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-20">August 20, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        4.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1338</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram No. 51 of
                    August 14, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d582-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith the text, with translation, of the note dated August 9, 1929,
                    which I received from the General <pb facs="0619" n="501" xml:id="pg501"/>
                    Secretariat of Foreign Affairs relative to the settlement of our claims in the
                    Spanish Zone of Morocco. Copy of the note has been sent to Tangier.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ogden H. Hammond</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d582-a1.xml" xpointer="d582-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
